{"name":"Canadian Fir","hex":"#415a53","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Firan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conifer of the genus Abies.","Any pinaceous conifer of related genera, especially a Douglas fir (Pseudotsuga) or a Scots pine (Pinus sylvestris)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abies balsamea","blocks":[{"text":"Abies balsamea or balsam fir is a North American fir, native to most of eastern and central Canada and the northeastern United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Abies_balsamea.jpg/330px-Abies_balsamea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abies_balsamea","wikidata":"Q428023"},{"title":"Canadians","blocks":[{"text":"Canadians are people identified with the country of Canada. This connection may be residential, legal, historical or cultural. For most Canadians, many of these connections exist and are collectively the source of their being Canadian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadians","wikidata":"Q1196645"},{"title":"Fir","blocks":[{"text":"Firs are coniferous trees belonging to the genus Abies in the family Pinaceae. There are approximately 48–65 extant species, found on mountains throughout much of North and Central America, Eurasia, and North Africa. The genus is most closely related to Keteleeria, a small genus confined to eastern Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG/330px-Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.w